# Pin LF for every text file. Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true,
# which checks the working tree out as CRLF. Git Bash tolerates CRLF scripts,
# but files the install links into ~/.claude would carry it too, and every
# edit made on Windows would round-trip through a line-ending conversion. On
# Linux and macOS checkouts are already LF, so this changes nothing there.
* text=auto eol=lf
